Also, the other races aren't randomly distributed across roles.  e.g.
gnomes will be a low % because they're often weak roles (e.g. healer);
elves and dwarves have a relatively high chance of being valks and
wizards (two of the easier classes, and both races fit those
particular roles well).

I'm not sure how much that would account for the differences (orcs are
likely to be barbarians or wizards, both easy) but with enough games
played it's probably a factor.

I used to play exclusively humans, I still favor them but I'll mix in
other races occasionally (elven rangers to toy with the extra
multishot, gnomish healers for pacifist games, etc).

